=== reschedule ===
  agent : Thank you for calling our clinic. I'm the virtual assistant. How can I help today?
  caller: Hi, I’d like to reschedule my upcoming check-up to next Wednesday afternoon — any doctor is fine.
  agent : Let me check what we can do. First, I'll need to verify your identity before accessing appointments. I can help with that. Please tell me your first name, your last name, and your date of birth, year, month, day, so I can verify your identity.
  caller: Alice Nguyen, born 1985, April 12.
  agent : Let me check your file and see what's available for Wednesday afternoon. Let me check the schedule for next Wednesday afternoon and find a few options. I found three options next Wednesday afternoon with Dr. Sarah Chen, 1 p.m., 2:15 p.m., or 3:30 p.m. Which time would you like to move your checkup to?
  caller: 2:15 p.m., please.
  agent : Let me update that appointment for you now. All set? Your general checkup is now on Wednesday, October 21st at 2:15 p.m. with Dr. Sarah Chen. If you need anything else, I can help with that too.
  caller: That's all, thank you.
  agent : Glad I could help. I'll close the call now. Take care and have a great day. Goodbye.

=== new_patient ===
  agent : Thank you for calling the clinic. I'm the virtual assistant. How can I help today?
  caller: Hi, this is Kevin Brown, born March 3, 1979. I haven't been to your clinic before — can I schedule an annual physical on a weekday morning within the next two weeks?
  agent : Let me check availability for that and get you set up. I can offer up to three options at a time. First, Monday, October 19th at 9 a.m. with Dr. Michael Patel. Next, Monday, October 19th at 9:45 a.m. Finally, Monday, October 19th at 10:30 a.m. Which time would you like?
  caller: I'll take the 9 a.m. appointment on Monday the 19th, please.
  agent : Got it. Let me confirm that booking for you now. You're booked for Monday, October 19th at 9 a.m. with Dr. Michael Patel for your annual physical. Please arrive a bit early and bring your health card and a list of current medications. If you need anything else, I can help.
  caller: No, that's all, thank you.
  agent : All right, I'll close things out for you now. You're very welcome. Have a great day. Goodbye.

=== faq_refill ===
  agent : Thank you for calling the clinic. I'm the virtual assistant. How can I help you today?
  caller: Hi, I'm Dan Miller — where should I park? Could you send a refill of my metformin to the Shoppers Drug Mart on King Street, and I'm fine leaving a message if needed.
  agent : Let me check that for you and pass along a refill request. You can park in the free lot behind the building and enter from Oak Lane. I've also left a message for Saf to handle the metformin refill to the Shoppers Drug Mart on King Street. They'll review it and get back to you, usually within one business day.
  caller: Great, thanks — I'll wait to hear from Saf.
  agent : Okay, I'll wrap this up for you now. You're all set. Have a good night and goodbye.

=== emergency ===
  agent : Thank you for calling our clinic. I'm the virtual assistant. How can I help you today?
  caller: I've had crushing chest pain and shortness of breath for about 20 minutes. I need the earliest appointment, please.
  agent : This sounds urgent. Please hang up and call 911 right now. Crushing chest pain and shortness of breath can be life-threatening and you need emergency care immediately. Do not wait for an appointment.
  caller: Okay, I'll call 911 right now.
  agent : I'm glad you're doing that. Please go ahead and call now. I'll end this call so emergency services can reach you. Take care. Ending the call so you can reach them.

=== human ===
  agent : Thank you for calling the clinic. I'm the virtual assistant. How can I help today?
  caller: Yes — there's a $150 charge on my bill from last week for a "lab service" I never received.
  agent : I'm sorry that happened. I can't handle billing disputes directly, but I can take a message for staff to review. Could I have your full name as it appears on your file?
  caller: It's Jordan Lee Matthews — that's J-O-R-D-A-N L-E-E M-A-T-T-H-E-W-S.
  agent : Okay, thanks. I'll take down a few details for the billing team, then I'll send it along. All set. I've sent your message to the billing team. They usually call back within one business day. If you'd like, you can also leave a callback number, or they can use the one on file.
  caller: No — I need to speak to a real person in billing right now. Please transfer me.
  agent : Got it. I'll connect you to a staff member who can help with billing. One moment, while I transfer you. Transferring now. Please stay on the line and a staff member will pick up as soon as they're available.

=== chinese ===
